Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||08-01-2001||01:25 PM||||i would think it would be worth it if you do it yourself.  you would only need to find a parts car with a goood tranny.  all the parts are there.  you have your hydrolic components and the lines,  then your tranny and cables.  i could buy new mounts because they arent too expensive.  new clutch of course.  flywheel of the donor car(or if it wont match find one from a forum member)  i would think the axles are different so swap them.  thats all i can think of mechanically.  i dont knwo what would be inolved electrically,  do you need to change the PCM or anything else.  i know the steering column is different but i think you can still use it(or take from your donor.  then you get into your clutch and brake switches and BS like that.  well the more i think about it maybe its not worth it. oh well i have a five speed already.  and i want an auto too so either way im happy.   =Þ<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000004||EdsB52||08-01-2001||01:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt boy:<BR><B>i was wondering if anyone has done a tranny swap from the auto to a 4 or 5spd??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've got the pedal assy out of the car, with steel clutch pedal if are going to do it. I could probably yank the line from the clutch master to the slave. But in reality, I would dissuade anyone form doing the swap.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-01-2001||07:46 PM||||Fore best results on a auto to stick, you need to rechip the ECM. <P>As for wire... At the very least you want to snip the wire from the ECM that used to goto the TC lockup to prevent it being shorted to a power line and frying the ECM. <P>I would do this up under the console. leave enough wire so that if you later want a shift light you can have one. <P>I don't know which wire it is on the V6 ECM connectors. You can trace it back from the TC lockup connector.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
